        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(extensions): remove dead QA and utility exports",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe production-mode Knip unused-export baseline still exposed private implementation details across QA and utility plugins. Those names looked like supported surfaces even though production code did not consume them.\n\nPart of #105736.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Remove 136 verified-unused extension entries from the shrink-only baseline.\n- Drop export modifiers from private helpers and types while preserving their internal runtime behavior.\n- Delete only declarations proven to have no production caller.\n- Preserve configured plugin entrypoints and contract-shaped `index.ts`, `api.ts`, and `runtime-api.ts` barrels.\n- Preserve exports reached by dynamic imports or valuable test coverage; no test files are deleted in this group.\n\nThe group covers ACPx, Copilot, Crabbox, Memory Core, Memory Wiki, OC Path, Ollama, OpenShell, Policy, QA Channel, QA Lab, QA Matrix, Workboard, and Workspaces.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime behavior change. Plugin maintainers get a smaller, more accurate private surface and 136 fewer extension entries in the enforced production dead-export baseline.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm test extensions/<id>` passed for every changed plugin listed above on Blacksmith Testbox; runs https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29216147217 and https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29216322533.\n- `pnpm test extensions/qa-matrix`: 222 tests passed; `pnpm test src/plugins/plugin-registry.test.ts`: 23 tests passed on https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29217107861 before the concurrent registry cleanup superseded that core-only portion.\n- `pnpm check:changed`: passed all selected core, extension, test, tooling, formatting, type, lint, guard, and cycle lanes on https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29216586783.\n- Final hosted Linux production regeneration and verification matched 4,734 entries after rebasing onto current main: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29229833018.\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` passed after restoring a production type export caught by the first CI attempt: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29227468485.\n- The final Linux artifact matches the committed baseline byte-for-byte; the diff contains no new baseline entry or core dead-export churn.\n- Exact-head autoreview against the final rebased diff: clean, no actionable findings (0.97 confidence); earlier focused reviews were also clean.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n",
